/* Generated by tools/bundle.mjs from CLAUDE.md, .claude/commands/ and .scrawl/hooks/. Don't edit by hand. */
window.Scrawl.templates = {
  "section": "## Scrawl work tracking",
  "protocol": "## Scrawl work tracking\n\nWork items live in `.scrawl/items/`, one Markdown file per item, named `0042-bug-short-slug.md`.\n\n- Never work on code without an item. Found something else? Create a new bug/idea item; don't silently expand scope.\n- Overviews: read `.scrawl/index.json` (one line per item). It can lag behind; the item files always win.\n- Header format: flat `key: value` lines between `---` fences. No nesting. Lists are `[a, b]`.\n  Keep fields you don't recognise exactly as they are.\n- Statuses: `proposed | backlog | ready | doing | review | resolved | done | wontfix`.\n  \"Claude's tray\" is `status: ready` + `assignee: claude`. After review the user may accept an item\n  (`resolved`); the board marks `review`/`resolved` items `done` (Shipped) once their PR is merged into main.\n- Picking up: set `status: doing`, `assignee: claude`, update `updated:`, add an Activity line.\n  Empty Acceptance section? Write 2-5 criteria from the Description, say so in Activity, and carry on.\n- Activity lines are append-only, newest last, one line each:\n  `- 2026-10-25 11:02 · claude · Picked up. Root cause: null email.`\n  Lines from `me` are the user's comments and instructions; read them before starting.\n- The board is not part of the project's git: `.scrawl/` is a separate worktree of its own\n  `scrawl-board` branch (set up once per clone by `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-setup`). Edit item files\n  there as usual, but never `git add` or commit them yourself; `scrawl-sync` commits and pushes the board.\n- Git: never commit to or push `main`. Each item gets its own branch `scrawl/<id>-<slug>`, pushed\n  with a PR (`gh pr create`); the user merges on GitHub. A feature is the exception: its stories\n  share the feature's branch, one commit each, and go out in one PR titled with every id\n  (`#3 #4 #5 Title`). See \"Resolving a feature\" in `.claude/commands/resolve.md`. Start every command with\n  `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync` — it fast-forwards `main` from GitHub (no manual pull) and saves the board.\n- Commits: start the message with the item number, e.g. `#42 Handle empty form`. Only a leading\n  `#N` links a commit to an item (GitHub's `(#12)` PR suffix is ignored). Merging the PR ships the card.\n  Commits and PRs carry code only.\n- Finishing: tick acceptance boxes you verified (`- [x]`), add a 1-3 sentence summary Activity line,\n  set `status: review`. Never set `resolved` or `done` — the user accepts items after review.\n- Creating an item: take `nextId` from `.scrawl/config.json`, then increment it there. File name is\n  `<id padded to 4>-<type>-<slug>.md`. Use this template:\n\n  ```\n  ---\n  id: 43\n  type: bug\n  title: Short title\n  status: backlog\n  assignee: me\n  labels: []\n  created: 2026-10-25T11:40\n  updated: 2026-10-25T11:40\n  ---\n  ## Description\n  What and why.\n\n  ## Acceptance\n  - [ ] Observable outcome\n\n  ## Activity\n  - 2026-10-25 11:40 · claude · Created while working on #42\n  ```\n\n  Types: `feature | story | bug | idea`. Bugs also get `severity: ant | beetle | cockroach | kraken`.\n  Leave `rank` out; the board ranks new items when they are dragged.\n- Timestamps are local time, minute precision (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM` in headers).\n- Don't edit `.scrawl/index.json` or `.scrawl/log/*`; the board and the git hook maintain them.\n",
  "files": {
    ".claude/commands/groom.md": "---\ndescription: Split oversized stories, fill missing acceptance, flag stale items\n---\nGroom the Scrawl board, following the \"Scrawl work tracking\" rules in CLAUDE.md.\nGrooming never changes an item's `status` and never touches code. Leave items in `resolved`,\n`done` and `wontfix` alone, and don't edit an item that is `doing` with `assignee: claude`\n(someone is working on it).\n\n1. Sync: `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync`. If it prints a warning, tell me.\n2. Read `.scrawl/index.json`, then the item files you need.\n3. Split oversized stories. A story is oversized when it has `size: L`, more than about six\n   Acceptance boxes, or clearly won't fit one Claude session.\n   - Create the smaller stories as new items (template and `nextId` rules in CLAUDE.md) with\n     `status: proposed`, `assignee: me`, the same `parent` as the original, a `size`, and the\n     original's acceptance boxes shared out between them.\n   - On the original, only append an Activity line:\n     `· claude · Groomed: proposed a split into #a, #b, #c. Reject this one once you accept them.`\n4. Fill missing acceptance. For each story or bug with an empty Acceptance section,\n   add 2-5 `- [ ]` boxes that follow from its Description, and append\n   `· claude · Groomed: added acceptance criteria. Edit them if I guessed wrong.`\n   If the Description is too thin to guess from, ask in an Activity line instead.\n   Skip features: their stories are their acceptance.\n5. Flag stale items: `doing` or `review` with `updated:` more than 14 days ago, or `ready` for more\n   than 30 days. Append `· claude · Groomed: stale since <date>. Still wanted?`\n   Don't change `updated:` on items you only flag, so they keep showing as stale, and skip items\n   whose last Activity line is already such a flag.\n6. Update `updated:` on every item whose content you changed (steps 3 and 4).\n7. Finish with a short list of what you split, filled and flagged, then run\n   `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync` to save the board.\n",
    ".claude/commands/inbox.md": "---\ndescription: Answer every @claude comment on the board\n---\nAnswer the comments that mention `@claude`, following the \"Scrawl work tracking\" rules in CLAUDE.md.\nAnswering never changes an item's `status` and never touches code.\n\n1. Sync: `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync`. If it prints a warning, tell me.\n2. Find the inbox: search `.scrawl/items/*.md` for Activity lines from `me` that mention\n   `@claude`. One is unanswered when no `claude` line comes after it in the same item.\n   If there are none, say the inbox is empty and stop.\n3. For each unanswered comment, oldest first, read the whole item (and its parent's Description\n   if it has one) and answer with one Activity line:\n   `- <now> · claude · @me <answer>`. Keep it to 1-3 sentences on one line.\n   - A question: answer it, looking at the code if you need to.\n   - A request to change the item itself (reword, split, add acceptance, re-parent): make the\n     change, then say what you changed.\n   - A request for code work: don't start it. Say how you'd approach it and that it's ready for\n     `/resolve <id>` once it's in Claude's tray. If it's new work, create a `proposed` item\n     for it and give its number.\n4. Update `updated:` on every item you answered.\n5. Finish with a short list (item number, what was asked, what you answered), then run\n   `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync` to save the board.\n",
    ".claude/commands/next.md": "---\ndescription: Take the top card from Claude's tray and resolve it\n---\nTake the next item from Claude's tray and resolve it.\n\n1. Sync first: `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync`.\n2. Find candidates: items in `.scrawl/items/` with `status: ready` and `assignee: claude`.\n   (`.scrawl/index.json` is a quick start, but confirm in the item files.)\n3. Pick the one with the lowest `rank` (plain string comparison; items without a rank come last,\n   then lowest id). If the tray is empty, say so and stop.\n   A story whose `parent` feature is also in the tray doesn't count: take the feature instead,\n   which resolves its stories with it.\n4. Tell me which item you picked, then follow `.claude/commands/resolve.md` for it exactly\n   (its sync step is already done). For a feature that means \"Resolving a feature\".\n",
    ".claude/commands/plan.md": "---\ndescription: Propose features and stories from project.md for the Plan view\nargument-hint: [feature <number>]\n---\nPlan this project into Scrawl items, following the \"Scrawl work tracking\" rules in CLAUDE.md.\nYou only propose: every item you create is `status: proposed`, and the user accepts or rejects\nit in the Plan view. Don't write code, and don't touch existing items except as said below.\n\n1. Sync: `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync`. If it prints a warning, tell me.\n2. Read `.scrawl/project.md`. If it has nothing under its headings, stop and tell me to fill in\n   the project wizard on the board first.\n3. Read `.scrawl/index.json` for what already exists (confirm in the item files when unsure).\n   Don't propose anything that duplicates an existing item, whatever its status.\n4. Scope (arguments: \"$ARGUMENTS\"):\n   - No arguments: propose the features (3-8 user-visible capabilities, covering the must-haves,\n     nothing from \"Out of scope\") and the stories for each.\n   - `feature <number>`: propose stories for that one existing feature only.\n     Use this on a big project to keep each run small.\n5. Create one file per item with the template in CLAUDE.md, taking each id from `nextId` in\n   `.scrawl/config.json` and incrementing it there before the next one. For every item:\n   - `status: proposed`, `assignee: me`, no `rank`.\n   - Stories: `parent: <feature id>` and `size: S | M | L`. S is under an hour, M fits one\n     Claude session, L needs splitting later with `/groom`. Aim for S and M.\n   - A short Description saying what and why. If an item needs another one first, end the\n     Description with `Depends on #N.`\n   - 2-5 Acceptance boxes, each an observable outcome you could check by hand.\n   - One Activity line: `- <now> · claude · Proposed by /plan`\n6. Finish with a short outline (features with their stories, ids and sizes) and tell me to\n   accept or reject them in the board's Plan view. Then run `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync`\n   to save the board.\n",
    ".claude/commands/release.md": "---\ndescription: Write the release notes for shipped items and tag main\nargument-hint: <version, e.g. 0.2.0>\n---\nRelease version $ARGUMENTS, following the \"Scrawl work tracking\" rules in CLAUDE.md.\nThis tags `main` but never commits to it; the release notes live on the board.\n\n1. Sync: `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync`. If it prints a warning, tell me and stop.\n2. Check the version: it must look like `1.2.3` (no leading `v`). No version given? Suggest one minor\n   above the newest file in `.scrawl/releases/` (or `0.1.0` if there is none), ask, and stop.\n   If the tag `v<version>` or `.scrawl/releases/v<version>.md` already exists, say so and stop.\n3. Collect the items: `status: done` and no `release:` field in the header. None? Say there's\n   nothing to release and stop.\n4. Write `.scrawl/releases/v<version>.md` in exactly this format (the board's Releases view\n   previews the same thing). Leave out empty groups. Within a group, sort by id. Types other than\n   these four count as Improvements.\n\n   ```\n   # v0.2.0\n\n   2026-10-26\n\n   ## Features\n   - #3 Planning: wizard, /plan and the Plan view\n\n   ## Improvements\n   - #4 Project wizard writes project.md\n\n   ## Bug fixes\n   - #21 Retry sync and hand-back when the open board writes mid-switch\n\n   ## Ideas\n   - #24 Accept a proposed feature together with its stories\n   ```\n\n   The date is today, local time.\n5. On every released item, add `release: <version>` to the header (keep every other line as it is)\n   and append `· claude · Released in v<version>`. Leave `updated:` alone, so the Shipped column\n   keeps its order.\n6. Tag the newest commit on main and push the tag:\n   `git tag -a v<version> main -m \"v<version>\"`, then `git push origin v<version>`.\n7. Run `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync` to save the board, then tell me the version, how many items it\n   has per group, and the tag.\n",
    ".claude/commands/resolve.md": "---\ndescription: Pick up a Scrawl item, implement it on a branch, open a PR, and move it to review\nargument-hint: <item number>\n---\nResolve Scrawl item #$ARGUMENTS, following the \"Scrawl work tracking\" rules in CLAUDE.md.\nNever commit to or push `main`. The user merges PRs on GitHub.\n\n1. Sync: `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync`. This pulls merged PRs from GitHub into `main` and saves the\n   board (its own `scrawl-board` branch). If it prints a warning, tell me.\n2. Find the item file: `.scrawl/items/` file whose name starts with the number padded to 4 digits\n   (e.g. #42 → `0042-*.md`). Read it fully, including Activity comments from `me`.\n   If it has a `parent`, skim the parent item's Description for context.\n   **If it is a feature, follow \"Resolving a feature\" below instead of steps 3-8.**\n3. Pick it up: set `status: doing`, `assignee: claude`, update `updated:`, append an Activity line\n   (`· claude · Picked up on branch scrawl/$ARGUMENTS-<slug>. <one-line plan>`). Save the file, then\n   `git switch -c scrawl/$ARGUMENTS-<slug> main` (short slug from the title). The board isn't on any\n   code branch, so switching never touches it.\n   If the Acceptance section is empty, write 2-5 `- [ ]` criteria that follow from the Description,\n   append `· claude · Added acceptance criteria; correct them at review if I guessed wrong.`, and carry on.\n4. Make a short plan, then implement. Keep scope to the Description and Acceptance criteria.\n   Anything else you notice becomes a new item, not extra work.\n5. Verify: run the tests if the project has them, otherwise check the acceptance criteria by hand.\n   If you can't make it work, append an Activity line explaining why, leave it in `doing`, and stop\n   (still do steps 7-8 with whatever is committed).\n6. Finish the item: tick the acceptance boxes you verified, append a 1-3 sentence summary Activity\n   line, set `status: review`, update `updated:`. Never set `resolved` or `done`.\n7. Commit the code only (never `.scrawl/`) with the message `#$ARGUMENTS <summary>`. Push the branch:\n   `git push -u origin scrawl/$ARGUMENTS-<slug>`.\n   Open the PR: `gh pr create --base main --title \"#$ARGUMENTS <summary>\" --body \"<what and why, how verified>\"`.\n8. Append an Activity line with the PR link (`· claude · PR: <url>`), then `git switch main` and\n   `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync` to save the board.\n\n## Resolving a feature\n\nA feature is done as a whole: all its stories on one branch, one commit per story, one PR.\n\nF1. Collect the stories: items with `parent: $ARGUMENTS` whose status is not `proposed`, `done`,\n    `resolved` or `wontfix`. Skip proposed ones (the user hasn't accepted them); mention them at the end.\n    Stories already in `review` were finished by an earlier run: leave them as they are.\nF2. Nothing to do from F1? Look at all of its stories before creating any:\n    - Some are `done` or `resolved` and none are open: the work is finished. Tell me (the feature\n      may just need accepting) and stop.\n    - Only proposed ones: tell me to accept or reject them in the Plan view, and stop.\n    - None at all (ignoring `wontfix`): split the feature into the stories it needs and create them\n      (template and `nextId` rules in CLAUDE.md) with `status: ready`, `assignee: claude`,\n      `parent: $ARGUMENTS`, a `size`, 2-5 acceptance boxes and the Activity line\n      `· claude · Created by /resolve $ARGUMENTS`. If it needs more than 6 new stories, don't create\n      them: list the split you'd make, ask me, and stop. It's probably two features.\nF3. Pick up the feature as in step 3 (fill its acceptance if empty), on branch\n    `scrawl/$ARGUMENTS-<slug>`. If that branch already exists (an earlier run stopped halfway),\n    switch to it instead of creating it.\nF4. For each story, in rank order (no rank last, then lowest id):\n    pick it up as in step 3 but stay on the feature's branch (say so in the Activity line, and fill\n    its acceptance if empty), implement and verify it as in steps 4-5, finish it as in step 6, then\n    commit with the message `#<story id> <summary>` and push\n    (`git push -u origin scrawl/$ARGUMENTS-<slug>`). Pushing after every story means a rerun of\n    `/resolve $ARGUMENTS` picks up where this one stopped.\n    If a story can't be made to work, or you have to stop (e.g. usage limits): leave that story and the\n    feature in `doing`, append an Activity line to the feature saying which stories are done and where\n    you stopped, push, `git switch main`, sync, and stop. Don't open the PR yet.\nF5. When every story is in `review`: tick the feature's acceptance boxes you verified, append a summary\n    Activity line and set it to `review`. Open one PR whose title starts with every id, feature first:\n    `gh pr create --base main --title \"#$ARGUMENTS #<story> #<story> <summary>\" --body \"<per story: what and how verified>\"`.\n    (A squash merge keeps only the title, so every id has to be in it for the cards to ship.)\nF6. Append `· claude · PR: <url>` to the feature and to each of its stories, then `git switch main`\n    and `sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync` to save the board.\n",
    ".scrawl/hooks/post-commit": "#!/bin/sh\n# Scrawl: record each commit so the board can link it to items (\"#42 ...\" in the message).\n# Runs from the repo root. Line format: shortsha|ISO date|author|subject\nlog=.scrawl/log/commits.txt\nfmt='%h|%cI|%an|%s'\n\n[ -d .scrawl/log ] || exit 0\n\nif [ -f \"$log\" ]; then\n  git log -1 --format=\"$fmt\" >> \"$log\"\nelse\n  # First run or fresh clone: backfill the whole history once.\n  git log --reverse --format=\"$fmt\" > \"$log\"\nfi\n\nsh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-main\n",
    ".scrawl/hooks/post-merge": "#!/bin/sh\n# Scrawl: a merge or pull may have brought branch work onto main.\n[ -d .scrawl/log ] || exit 0\nsh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-main\n",
    ".scrawl/hooks/scrawl-main": "#!/bin/sh\n# Scrawl: list the commits on the main branch so the board can mark finished items as Shipped.\n# Called by post-commit, post-merge and scrawl-sync. Writes \"shortsha|subject\", newest first,\n# to .scrawl/log/main.txt. Subjects matter: squash and rebase merges give the work new shas.\nout=.scrawl/log/main.txt\n\n[ -d .scrawl/log ] || exit 0\n\nmain=\nfor b in main master; do\n  if git rev-parse --verify -q \"refs/heads/$b\" >/dev/null; then main=$b; break; fi\ndone\n[ -n \"$main\" ] || exit 0\n\ngit log --format='%h|%s' --max-count=2000 \"$main\" > \"$out.tmp\" && mv -f \"$out.tmp\" \"$out\"\n",
    ".scrawl/hooks/scrawl-setup": "#!/bin/sh\n# Scrawl: keep the board out of your project's git. Run once per clone: sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-setup\n#\n# The board (.scrawl/) lives on its own branch, scrawl-board, which shares no history with your code.\n# It is checked out as a separate git worktree at .scrawl/ and listed in .git/info/exclude, so card\n# moves never show up in your project's `git status`, diffs or PRs, and switching branches never\n# touches the board. scrawl-sync commits and pushes the board branch for you.\n#\n# A plain .scrawl/ folder is moved onto the branch (on top of it, if the branch already exists).\n# On a fresh clone .scrawl/ isn't there yet; fetch it first: git worktree add .scrawl scrawl-board\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../..\" || exit 1\nboard=scrawl-board\n\nexclude=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/info/exclude\"\nmkdir -p \"$(dirname \"$exclude\")\"\ngrep -qx '/.scrawl/' \"$exclude\" 2>/dev/null || printf '/.scrawl/\\n' >> \"$exclude\"\ngit config core.hooksPath .scrawl/hooks\n\nif [ -e .scrawl/.git ]; then\n  echo \"scrawl-setup: the board is on branch $(git -C .scrawl symbolic-ref -q --short HEAD)\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n[ -d .scrawl ] || { echo \"scrawl-setup: no .scrawl/ folder here\" >&2; exit 1; }\nif [ -n \"$(git ls-files -- .scrawl | head -n 1)\" ]; then\n  echo \"scrawl-setup: .scrawl/ is still tracked by $(git symbolic-ref -q --short HEAD || echo HEAD).\" >&2\n  echo \"  Untrack it first (git rm -r -q --cached .scrawl), commit that, then run this again.\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# The board branch keeps its own LF rule and leaves out everything Scrawl rebuilds.\n[ -f .scrawl/.gitattributes ] || printf '* text=auto eol=lf\\n' > .scrawl/.gitattributes\n[ -f .scrawl/.gitignore ] || printf '%s\\n' '# Rebuilt by the board and the git hooks' \\\n  index.json log/commits.txt log/main.txt log/main.txt.tmp > .scrawl/.gitignore\n\nparent=\nif git rev-parse --verify -q \"refs/heads/$board\" >/dev/null; then\n  parent=$(git rev-parse \"refs/heads/$board\")\nelif git rev-parse --verify -q \"refs/remotes/origin/$board\" >/dev/null; then\n  parent=$(git rev-parse \"refs/remotes/origin/$board\")\nfi\n\n# Commit the folder as it is onto the board branch, using a throwaway index.\ngitdir=$(git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir)\nidx=\"$gitdir/scrawl-setup.index\"\nrm -f \"$idx\"\ncommit=$(\n  cd .scrawl || exit 1\n  export GIT_DIR=\"$gitdir\" GIT_WORK_TREE=. GIT_INDEX_FILE=\"$idx\"\n  if [ -n \"$parent\" ]; then git read-tree \"$parent\"; else git read-tree --empty; fi\n  git add -A . || exit 1\n  git ls-files -ci --exclude-standard | while IFS= read -r f; do git rm -q --cached -- \"$f\"; done\n  git ls-files -- hooks | while IFS= read -r f; do git update-index --chmod=+x -- \"$f\"; done\n  tree=$(git write-tree) || exit 1\n  if [ -n \"$parent\" ] && [ \"$tree\" = \"$(git rev-parse \"$parent^{tree}\")\" ]; then echo \"$parent\"; exit 0; fi\n  if [ -n \"$parent\" ]; then git commit-tree \"$tree\" -p \"$parent\" -m \"Board: moved onto its own branch\"\n  else git commit-tree \"$tree\" -m \"Board: moved onto its own branch\"; fi\n)\nrc=$?\nrm -f \"$idx\"\n[ $rc -eq 0 ] && [ -n \"$commit\" ] || { echo \"scrawl-setup: couldn't commit the board\" >&2; exit 1; }\ngit update-ref \"refs/heads/$board\" \"$commit\"\n\n# Turn the folder into a worktree of the branch where it stands (its files already match the branch):\n# make an empty worktree elsewhere, hand its .git link to .scrawl/, and let git repair the paths.\n# Nothing is moved, so the open board keeps working and rebuilt files stay put.\ntmp=\"$gitdir/scrawl-setup/.scrawl\"\nrm -rf \"$gitdir/scrawl-setup\"\nif ! git worktree add -q --no-checkout \"$tmp\" \"$board\"; then\n  echo \"scrawl-setup: couldn't make a worktree for $board; .scrawl/ is unchanged\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\nmv \"$tmp/.git\" .scrawl/.git\nrm -rf \"$gitdir/scrawl-setup\"\ngit worktree repair .scrawl >/dev/null 2>&1\ngit -C .scrawl reset -q\necho \"scrawl-setup: the board is now on branch $board (scrawl-sync commits and pushes it)\"\n",
    ".scrawl/hooks/scrawl-sync": "#!/bin/sh\n# Scrawl: bring local main up to date with GitHub, so merged PRs show up as Shipped on the board,\n# and save the board. Claude runs this at the start of /resolve and /next; it is safe to run any time.\n#\n# The board (.scrawl/) is its own worktree on the scrawl-board branch (see scrawl-setup), so main\n# and the board never get in each other's way. Board edits (moves, comments, Claude's item edits)\n# are committed on scrawl-board and pushed; your code branches and PRs never carry them.\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../..\" || exit 1\nremote=origin\nboard=scrawl-board\n\nmain=\nfor b in main master; do\n  if git rev-parse --verify -q \"refs/heads/$b\" >/dev/null; then main=$b; break; fi\ndone\n\nonline=\nif git remote get-url \"$remote\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  if git fetch -q --prune \"$remote\"; then online=1\n  else echo \"scrawl-sync: couldn't reach $remote; the board may be behind GitHub\" >&2; fi\nfi\n\nsync_main() {\n  [ -n \"$main\" ] && [ -n \"$online\" ] || return 0\n  target=\"$remote/$main\"\n  git rev-parse --verify -q \"$target\" >/dev/null || return 0\n  [ \"$(git rev-parse \"$main\")\" = \"$(git rev-parse \"$target\")\" ] && return 0\n  if ! git merge-base --is-ancestor \"$main\" \"$target\"; then\n    echo \"scrawl-sync: local $main has commits that $target doesn't; left it alone\" >&2\n    return 0\n  fi\n  if [ \"$(git symbolic-ref -q --short HEAD)\" = \"$main\" ]; then\n    git merge -q --ff-only \"$target\" || echo \"scrawl-sync: couldn't fast-forward $main; the board may be behind GitHub\" >&2\n  else\n    # Another branch is checked out: just move the main ref forward.\n    git fetch -q \"$remote\" \"$main:$main\" || echo \"scrawl-sync: couldn't fast-forward $main\" >&2\n  fi\n}\n\n# Commit whatever changed on the board, then line it up with GitHub's copy and push.\nsync_board() {\n  if [ ! -e .scrawl/.git ]; then\n    [ -d .scrawl ] && echo \"scrawl-sync: .scrawl/ isn't on its own branch yet; run: sh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-setup\" >&2\n    return 0\n  fi\n  g() { git -C .scrawl \"$@\"; }\n  g add -A\n  g diff --cached --quiet || g commit -q --no-verify -m \"Board: $(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')\"\n  [ -n \"$online\" ] || return 0\n  theirs=\"refs/remotes/$remote/$board\"\n  if g rev-parse --verify -q \"$theirs\" >/dev/null && ! g merge-base --is-ancestor \"$theirs\" HEAD; then\n    # Edited on another machine too. One file per item keeps real conflicts rare.\n    if ! g rebase -q --autostash \"$theirs\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n      g rebase --abort >/dev/null 2>&1\n      echo \"scrawl-sync: the board changed here and on $remote in the same place; kept the local board, not pushed\" >&2\n      return 0\n    fi\n  fi\n  g push -q -u \"$remote\" \"HEAD:refs/heads/$board\" 2>/dev/null ||\n    echo \"scrawl-sync: couldn't push the board to $remote\" >&2\n}\n\nsync_main\nif [ -n \"$main\" ] && [ -e .scrawl/.git ] && git cat-file -e \"$main:.scrawl\" 2>/dev/null; then\n  echo \"scrawl-sync: $main still tracks .scrawl/; merge the PR that moves the board onto its own branch,\" >&2\n  echo \"  and don't switch to $main until then (it would write old board files over the live board).\" >&2\nfi\n\nsync_board\nsh .scrawl/hooks/scrawl-main\nexit 0\n"
  }
};
